VTID-03790 — commands.log
==========================

## Background: the live diff that motivated this VTID

Ran two real live sessions against staging (preview-aws-gateway.vitanaland.com)
as the documented e2e-test@vitana.dev account (see platform CLAUDE.md's
sanctioned testing exception): one with guided_topic_id set (blocked by
nova_validation, matching every prior report in the VTID-03674->03786
chain), one an ordinary open (succeeded). Pulled both sessions'
nova_instruction_debug_dump diag events (VTID-03787 instrumentation,
metadata->>'stage'='nova_instruction_debug_dump') from oasis_events and
diffed the literal instruction_text between them.

Finding: the guided session's instruction carried a
"SPOKEN FIRST UTTERANCE — REQUIRED VERBATIM" block (from
buildVertexWakeBriefBlock, live-session-controller.ts) containing:

  "So, das war „Was ist Vitanaland". Hast du Fragen dazu, oder sollen wir
  direkt gemeinsam loslegen?"

-- German guillemet quotes around the dynamic topic title, nested inside the
wrapper's own outer straight quotes. The GUIDE-MODUS block repeated the
pattern around practice_target and the „ja"/„mach das"/„okay" exemplar
words. Reported plainly to the user with this exact evidence; user replied
"Go ahead and build the fix."

## Locating every site

$ grep -rn '„' services/gateway/src/orb/live/instruction/guided-topic-narration-prompt.ts
-> 7 sites across 4 functions (buildGuidedTopicNarrationOpenerLine,
   buildGuidedTopicSpokenLesson, buildGuidedTopicPostNarrationLine,
   buildGuidedTopicNarrationBlock x2 branches)

Confirmed English branches carry the structurally identical defect (plain
straight quotes, nested inside buildVertexWakeBriefBlock's own outer
straight-quote wrapper) via direct read of live-session-controller.ts:580-644.

## Fix

Removed every guillemet/straight-quote wrap around dynamic content (topic
title, practice_target, short exemplar words) across all 4 functions x both
language branches. Practice-target references kept their existing plain
parentheses (`(${content.practice_target})`) with only the quote marks
inside them removed. One minor grammar adjustment (German "heißt" ->
"bedeutet") to keep the sentence readable once the surrounding quotes were
gone.

$ grep -n '„|”|"\$\{' services/gateway/src/orb/live/instruction/guided-topic-narration-prompt.ts
(no matches -- confirms every nested-quote site is gone)

## New regression tests

Added `describe('VTID-03790: no nested quotation marks around dynamic
content (Nova content-filter fix)')` to
test/orb/live/instruction/guided-topic-narration-prompt.test.ts -- 6 new
tests: one per builder function (opener line, spoken-lesson fallback,
post-narration line, narration block x2 branches) asserting no `"`/`„`/`"`
character appears in the output, plus one meaning-preservation test
confirming the topic title/practice target are still present as plain text.

$ cd services/gateway && npx jest test/orb/live/instruction/guided-topic-narration-prompt.test.ts
PASS -- 26/26 (20 pre-existing + 6 new)
(outputs/jest-scoped-fixed.txt)

